cim:BilateralExchangeActor a owl:Class;
                           rdfs:comment "BilateralExchangeActor describes an actor that provides ICCP data, consumes ICCP data or both. The ICCP data provider lists the data it makes available to an ICCP data consumer. This data is described by ProvidedBilateralPoints. The relation between an ICCP data provider and a consumer is established by a BilateralExchangeAgreement. It is up to the ICCP data consumer to select what ProvidedBilateralPoints to use. The selection made is not described in this information model."@en;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "BilateralExchangeActor"@en;
                           rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject;
                           cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.ICCPConfiguration";
                           cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:BilateralExchangeActor.ProviderBilateralExchange a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                     rdfs:comment "Agreement to information provider."@en;
                                                     rdfs:domain cim:BilateralExchangeActor;
                                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                     rdfs:label "ProviderBilateralExchange"@en;
                                                     rdfs:range cim:BilateralExchangeAgreement.
cim:BilateralExchangeAgreement a owl:Class;
                               rdfs:comment "This is the representation of the information exchange agreement between peers."@en;
