cim:Equipment.aggregate a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                        rdfs:comment "The aggregate flag provides an alternative way of representing an aggregated (equivalent) element. It is applicable in cases when the dedicated classes for equivalent equipment do not have all of the attributes necessary to represent the required level of detail. In case the flag is set to �true� the single instance of equipment represents multiple pieces of equipment that have been modelled together as an aggregate equivalent obtained by a network reduction procedure. Examples would be power transformers or synchronous machines operating in parallel modelled as a single aggregate power transformer or aggregate synchronous machine. The attribute is not used for EquivalentBranch, EquivalentShunt and EquivalentInjection."@en;
                        rdfs:domain cim:Equipment;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "aggregate"@en;
                        rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Equipment.inService a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                        rdfs:comment "Specifies the availability of the equipment. True means the equipment is available for topology processing, which determines if the equipment is energized or not. False means that the equipment is treated by network applications as if it is not in the model."@en;
                        rdfs:domain cim:Equipment;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "inService"@en;
                        rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Equipment.networkAnalysisEnabled a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                     rdfs:comment "The equipment is enabled to participate in network analysis. If unspecified, the value is assumed to be true."@en;
                                     rdfs:domain cim:Equipment;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                     rdfs:label "networkAnalysisEnabled"@en;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Equipment.normallyInService a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                rdfs:comment "Specifies the availability of the equipment under normal operating conditions. True means the equipment is available for topology processing, which determines if the equipment is energized or not. False means that the equipment is treated by network applications as if it is not in the model."@en;
                                rdfs:domain cim:Equipment;
                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                rdfs:label "normallyInService"@en;
                                rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:EquipmentContainer a owl:Class;
                       rdfs:comment "A modelling construct to provide a root class for containing equipment."@en;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                       rdfs:label "EquipmentContainer"@en;
                       rdfs:subClassOf cim:ConnectivityNodeContainer;
                       cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Core";
                       cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquipmentContainer.AdditionalGroupedEquipment a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                  rdfs:comment "The additonal contained equipment. The equipment belong to the equipment container. The equipment is contained in another equipment container, but also grouped with this equipment container. Examples include when a switch contained in a substation is also desired to be grouped with a line contianer or when a switch is included in a secondary substation and also grouped in a feeder."@en;
                                                  rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentContainer;
                                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                  rdfs:label "AdditionalGroupedEquipment"@en;
                                                  rdfs:range cim:Equipment.
cim:EquipmentContainer.Equipments a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                  rdfs:comment "Contained equipment."@en;
                                  rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentContainer;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                  rdfs:label "Equipments"@en;
                                  rdfs:range cim:Equipment.
cim:EquipmentFault a owl:Class;
                   rdfs:comment "A fault applied at the terminal, external to the equipment. This class is not used to specify faults internal to the equipment."@en;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                   rdfs:label "EquipmentFault"@en;
                   rdfs:subClassOf cim:Fault;
                   cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Faults";
                   cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquipmentFault.Terminal a owl:ObjectProperty;
                            rdfs:comment "The terminal connecting to the bus to which the fault is applied."@en;
                            rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentFault;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "Terminal"@en;
                            rdfs:range cim:Terminal.
cim:EquipmentLimitSeriesComponent a owl:Class;
                                  rdfs:comment "This represents one instance of an equipment that contributes to the calculation of an operational limit."@en;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                  rdfs:label "EquipmentLimitSeriesComponent"@en;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject;
                                  cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.InfIEC61970.InfOperationalLimits";
                                  cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
cim:EquipmentLimitSeriesComponent.Equipment a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                            rdfs:comment "Equipment contributing toward the series limit. The reference here is to Equipment rather than a specific limit on the equipment so the grouping can be reused for multiple limits of different types on the same instance of equipment."@en;
                                            rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentLimitSeriesComponent;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                            rdfs:label "Equipment"@en;
                                            rdfs:range cim:Equipment.
cim:EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule a owl:Class;
                                    rdfs:comment "Represents an equipment unavailability schedule."@en;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule"@en;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject;
                                    cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.InfIEC61970.InfAvailabilityPlans";
                                    cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
cim:EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule.m_Equipment a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                rdfs:comment "The equipment associated with this unavailability schedule."@en;
                                                rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                rdfs:label "m_Equipment"@en;
                                                rdfs:range cim:Equipment.
cim:EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule.m_UnavailablitySchedule a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                            rdfs:comment "The unavailability schedule associated with this equipment."@en;
                                                            rdfs:domain cim:EquipmentUnavailabilitySchedule;
                                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                            rdfs:label "m_UnavailablitySchedule"@en;
                                                            rdfs:range cim:UnavailablitySchedule.
cim:EquivalentBranch a owl:Class;
                     rdfs:comment "The class represents equivalent branches. In cases where a transformer phase shift is modelled and the EquivalentBranch is spanning the same nodes, the impedance quantities for the EquivalentBranch shall consider the needed phase shift."@en;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                     rdfs:label "EquivalentBranch"@en;
                     rdfs:subClassOf cim:EquivalentEquipment;
                     cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Equivalents";
                     cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquivalentBranch.negativeR12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Negative sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "negativeR12"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.negativeR21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Negative sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "negativeR21"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.negativeX12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Negative sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "negativeX12"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.negativeX21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Negative sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage: EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "negativeX21"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.positiveR12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2 . Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "positiveR12"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.positiveR21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "positiveR21"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.positiveX12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "positiveX12"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.positiveX21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "positiveX21"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.r a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                       rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series resistance of the reduced branch."@en;
                       rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                       rdfs:label "r"@en;
                       rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.r21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                         rdfs:comment "Resistance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1 .Used for steady state power flow. This attribute is optional and represent unbalanced network such as off-nominal phase shifter. If only EquivalentBranch.r is given, then EquivalentBranch.r21 is assumed equal to EquivalentBranch.r. Usage rule : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                         rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "r21"@en;
                         rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.x a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                       rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series reactance of the reduced branch."@en;
                       rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                       rdfs:label "x"@en;
                       rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.x21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                         rdfs:comment "Reactance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for steady state power flow. This attribute is optional and represents an unbalanced network such as off-nominal phase shifter. If only EquivalentBranch.x is given, then EquivalentBranch.x21 is assumed equal to EquivalentBranch.x. Usage rule: EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                         rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "x21"@en;
                         rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.zeroR12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Zero sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "zeroR12"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.zeroR21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Zero sequence series resistance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "zeroR21"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.zeroX12 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Zero sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 1 to terminal sequence 2. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "zeroX12"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentBranch.zeroX21 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Zero sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909. Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "zeroX21"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentEquipment a owl:Class;
                        rdfs:comment "The class represents equivalent objects that are the result of a network reduction. The class is the base for equivalent objects of different types."@en;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "EquivalentEquipment"@en;
                        rdfs:subClassOf cim:ConductingEquipment;
                        cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Equivalents";
                        cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquivalentInjection a owl:Class;
                        rdfs:comment "This class represents equivalent injections (generation or load). Voltage regulation is allowed only at the point of connection."@en;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "EquivalentInjection"@en;
                        rdfs:subClassOf cim:EquivalentEquipment;
                        cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Equivalents";
                        cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquivalentInjection.maxP a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Maximum active power of the injection."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "maxP"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:ActivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.maxQ a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Maximum reactive power of the injection. Used for modelling of infeed for load flow exchange. Not used for short circuit modelling. If maxQ and minQ are not used ReactiveCapabilityCurve can be used."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "maxQ"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:ReactivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.minP a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Minimum active power of the injection."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "minP"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:ActivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.minQ a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "Minimum reactive power of the injection. Used for modelling of infeed for load flow exchange. Not used for short circuit modelling. If maxQ and minQ are not used ReactiveCapabilityCurve can be used."@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "minQ"@en;
                             rdfs:range cim:ReactivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.p a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Equivalent active power injection. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. Starting value for steady state solutions."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "p"@en;
                          rdfs:range cim:ActivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.q a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Equivalent reactive power injection. Load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a node. Starting value for steady state solutions."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "q"@en;
                          rdfs:range cim:ReactivePower.
cim:EquivalentInjection.r a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Positive sequence resistance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "r"@en;
                          rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentInjection.r0 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "Zero sequence resistance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                           rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "r0"@en;
                           rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentInjection.r2 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "Negative sequence resistance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                           rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "r2"@en;
                           rdfs:range cim:Resistance.
cim:EquivalentInjection.regulationCapability a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                             rdfs:comment "Specifies whether or not the EquivalentInjection has the capability to regulate the local voltage. If true the EquivalentInjection can regulate. If false the EquivalentInjection cannot regulate. ReactiveCapabilityCurve can only be associated with EquivalentInjection if the flag is true."@en;
                                             rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                             rdfs:label "regulationCapability"@en;
                                             rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:EquivalentInjection.regulationStatus a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                         rdfs:comment "Specifies the regulation status of the EquivalentInjection. True is regulating. False is not regulating."@en;
                                         rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "regulationStatus"@en;
                                         rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:EquivalentInjection.regulationTarget a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                         rdfs:comment "The target voltage for voltage regulation. The attribute shall be a positive value."@en;
                                         rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "regulationTarget"@en;
                                         rdfs:range cim:Voltage.
cim:EquivalentInjection.x a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Positive sequence reactance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "x"@en;
                          rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentInjection.x0 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "Zero sequence reactance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                           rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "x0"@en;
                           rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentInjection.x2 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "Negative sequence reactance. Used to represent Extended-Ward (IEC 60909). Usage : Extended-Ward is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange."@en;
                           rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentInjection;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "x2"@en;
                           rdfs:range cim:Reactance.
cim:EquivalentNetwork a owl:Class;
                      rdfs:comment "A class that groups electrical equivalents, including internal nodes, of a network that has been reduced. The ConnectivityNodes contained in the equivalent are intended to reflect internal nodes of the equivalent. The boundary Connectivity nodes where the equivalent connects outside itself are not contained by the equivalent."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "EquivalentNetwork"@en;
                      rdfs:subClassOf cim:ConnectivityNodeContainer;
                      cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Equivalents";
                      cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquivalentNetwork.EquivalentEquipments a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                           rdfs:comment "The associated reduced equivalents."@en;
                                           rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentNetwork;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                           rdfs:label "EquivalentEquipments"@en;
                                           rdfs:range cim:EquivalentEquipment.
cim:EquivalentShunt a owl:Class;
                    rdfs:comment "The class represents equivalent shunts."@en;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                    rdfs:label "EquivalentShunt"@en;
                    rdfs:subClassOf cim:EquivalentEquipment;
                    cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Equivalents";
                    cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:EquivalentShunt.b a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "Positive sequence shunt susceptance."@en;
                      rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentShunt;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "b"@en;
                      rdfs:range cim:Susceptance.
cim:EquivalentShunt.g a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "Positive sequence shunt conductance."@en;
                      rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentShunt;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "g"@en;
                      rdfs:range cim:Conductance.
cim:ExcAC1A a owl:Class;
            rdfs:comment "Modified IEEE AC1A alternator-supplied rectifier excitation system with different rate feedback source."@en;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
            rdfs:label "ExcAC1A"@en;
            rdfs:subClassOf cim:ExcitationSystemDynamics;
            cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Dynamics.StandardModels.ExcitationSystemDynamics";
            cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:ExcAC1A.hvlvgates a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "Indicates if both HV gate and LV gate are active (HVLVgates). true = gates are used false = gates are not used. Typical value = true."@en;
                      rdfs:domain cim:ExcAC1A;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "hvlvgates"@en;
                      rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:ExcAC1A.ka a owl:DatatypeProperty;
               rdfs:comment "Voltage regulator gain (Ka) (greater than 0). Typical value = 400."@en;
               rdfs:domain cim:ExcAC1A;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
               rdfs:label "ka"@en;
               rdfs:range cim:PU.
cim:ExcAC1A.kc a owl:DatatypeProperty;
               rdfs:comment "Rectifier loading factor proportional to commutating reactance (Kc) (>= 0). Typical value = 0,2."@en;
               rdfs:domain cim:ExcAC1A;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
               rdfs:label "kc"@en;
               rdfs:range cim:PU.
cim:ExcAC1A.kd a owl:DatatypeProperty;
               rdfs:comment "Demagnetizing factor, a function of exciter alternator reactances (Kd) (>= 0). Typical value = 0,38."@en;
               rdfs:domain cim:ExcAC1A;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
               rdfs:label "kd"@en;
               rdfs:range cim:PU.
cim:ExcAC1A.ke a owl:DatatypeProperty;
               rdfs:comment "Exciter constant related to self-excited field (Ke). Typical value = 1."@en;
               rdfs:domain cim:ExcAC1A;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
               rdfs:label "ke"@en;
               rdfs:range cim:PU.
