cim:Quality61850 a owl:Class;
                 rdfs:comment "Quality flags in this class are as defined in IEC 61850, except for estimatorReplaced, which has been included in this class for convenience."@en;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                 rdfs:label "Quality61850"@en;
                 cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Meas";
                 cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:Quality61850.badReference a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                              rdfs:comment "Measurement value may be incorrect due to a reference being out of calibration."@en;
                              rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                              rdfs:label "badReference"@en;
                              rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.estimatorReplaced a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                   rdfs:comment "Value has been replaced by State Estimator. estimatorReplaced is not an IEC61850 quality bit but has been put in this class for convenience."@en;
                                   rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                   rdfs:label "estimatorReplaced"@en;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.failure a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                         rdfs:comment "This identifier indicates that a supervision function has detected an internal or external failure, e.g. communication failure."@en;
                         rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "failure"@en;
                         rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.oldData a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                         rdfs:comment "Measurement value is old and possibly invalid, as it has not been successfully updated during a specified time interval."@en;
                         rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "oldData"@en;
                         rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.operatorBlocked a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Measurement value is blocked and hence unavailable for transmission."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "operatorBlocked"@en;
                                 rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.oscillatory a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                             rdfs:comment """To prevent some overload of the communication it is sensible to detect and suppress oscillating (fast changing) binary inputs. If a signal changes in a defined time twice in the same direction (from 0 to 1 or from 1 to 0) then oscillation is detected and the detail quality identifier \"oscillatory\" is set. If it is detected a configured numbers of transient changes could be passed by. In this time the validity status \"questionable\" is set. If after this defined numbers of changes the signal is still in the oscillating state the value shall be set either to the opposite state of the previous stable value or to a defined default value. In this case the validity status \"questionable\" is reset and \"invalid\" is set as long as the signal is oscillating. If it is configured such that no transient changes should be passed by then the validity status \"invalid\" is set immediately in addition to the detail quality identifier \"oscillatory\" (used for status information only)."""@en;
                             rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "oscillatory"@en;
                             rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.outOfRange a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                            rdfs:comment "Measurement value is beyond a predefined range of value."@en;
                            rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "outOfRange"@en;
                            rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.overFlow a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Measurement value is beyond the capability of being represented properly. For example, a counter value overflows from maximum count back to a value of zero."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "overFlow"@en;
                          rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.source a owl:ObjectProperty;
                        rdfs:comment "Source gives information related to the origin of a value. The value may be acquired from the process, defaulted or substituted."@en;
                        rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "source"@en;
                        rdfs:range cim:Source.
cim:Quality61850.suspect a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                         rdfs:comment "A correlation function has detected that the value is not consistent with other values. Typically set by a network State Estimator."@en;
                         rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "suspect"@en;
                         rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.test a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "Measurement value is transmitted for test purposes."@en;
                      rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "test"@en;
                      rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:Quality61850.validity a owl:ObjectProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "Validity of the measurement value."@en;
                          rdfs:domain cim:Quality61850;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                          rdfs:label "validity"@en;
                          rdfs:range cim:Validity.
cim:RaiseLowerCommand a owl:Class;
                      rdfs:comment "An analog control that increases or decreases a set point value with pulses. Unless otherwise specified, one pulse moves the set point by one."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "RaiseLowerCommand"@en;
                      rdfs:subClassOf cim:AnalogControl;
                      cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Meas";
                      cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RaiseLowerCommand.ValueAliasSet a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                    rdfs:comment "The ValueAliasSet used for translation of a Control value to a name."@en;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RaiseLowerCommand;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "ValueAliasSet"@en;
                                    rdfs:range cim:ValueAliasSet.
cim:RatioTapChanger a owl:Class;
                    rdfs:comment "A tap changer that changes the voltage ratio impacting the voltage magnitude but not the phase angle across the transformer. Angle sign convention (general): Positive value indicates a positive phase shift from the winding where the tap is located to the other winding (for a two- winding transformer)."@en;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                    rdfs:label "RatioTapChanger"@en;
                    rdfs:subClassOf cim:TapChanger;
                    cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                    cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RatioTapChanger.RatioTapChangerTable a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                         rdfs:comment "The tap ratio table for this ratio tap changer."@en;
                                         rdfs:domain cim:RatioTapChanger;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "RatioTapChangerTable"@en;
                                         rdfs:range cim:RatioTapChangerTable.
cim:RatioTapChanger.stepVoltageIncrement a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                         rdfs:comment "Tap step increment, in per cent of rated voltage of the power transformer end, per step position. When the increment is negative, the voltage decreases when the tap step increases."@en;
                                         rdfs:domain cim:RatioTapChanger;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "stepVoltageIncrement"@en;
                                         rdfs:range cim:PerCent.
cim:RatioTapChanger.tculControlMode a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                    rdfs:comment "Specifies the regulation control mode (voltage or reactive) of the RatioTapChanger."@en;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RatioTapChanger;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "tculControlMode"@en;
                                    rdfs:range cim:TransformerControlMode.
cim:RatioTapChangerTable a owl:Class;
                         rdfs:comment "Describes a curve for how the voltage magnitude and impedance varies with the tap step."@en;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "RatioTapChangerTable"@en;
                         rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject;
                         cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                         cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RatioTapChangerTablePoint a owl:Class;
                              rdfs:comment "Describes each tap step in the ratio tap changer tabular curve."@en;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                              rdfs:label "RatioTapChangerTablePoint"@en;
                              rdfs:subClassOf cim:TapChangerTablePoint;
                              cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                              cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RatioTapChangerTablePoint.RatioTapChangerTable a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                   rdfs:comment "Table of this point."@en;
                                                   rdfs:domain cim:RatioTapChangerTablePoint;
                                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                   rdfs:label "RatioTapChangerTable"@en;
                                                   rdfs:range cim:RatioTapChangerTable.
cim:Reactance a rdfs:Datatype;
              rdfs:comment "Reactance (imaginary part of impedance), at rated frequency."@en;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
              rdfs:label "Reactance"@en;
              owl:equivalentClass xsd:float;
              cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Domain";
              cimdoc:packageTier "Normative";
              cimdoc:unitSymbol cim:UnitSymbol.ohm.
cim:ReactancePerLength a rdfs:Datatype;
                       rdfs:comment "Reactance (imaginary part of impedance) per unit of length, at rated frequency."@en;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                       rdfs:label "ReactancePerLength"@en;
                       owl:equivalentClass xsd:float;
                       cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Domain";
                       cimdoc:packageTier "Normative";
                       cimdoc:unitMultiplier cim:UnitMultiplier.none;
                       cimdoc:unitSymbol cim:UnitSymbol.ohmPerm.
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve a owl:Class;
                            rdfs:comment "Reactive power rating envelope versus the synchronous machine's active power, in both the generating and motoring modes. For each active power value there is a corresponding high and low reactive power limit value. Typically there will be a separate curve for each coolant condition, such as hydrogen pressure. The Y1 axis values represent reactive minimum and the Y2 axis values represent reactive maximum."@en;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "ReactiveCapabilityCurve"@en;
                            rdfs:subClassOf cim:Curve;
                            cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                            cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve.EquivalentInjection a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                rdfs:comment "The equivalent injection using this reactive capability curve."@en;
                                                rdfs:domain cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                rdfs:label "EquivalentInjection"@en;
                                                rdfs:range cim:EquivalentInjection.
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve.InitiallyUsedBySynchronousMachines a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                               rdfs:comment "Synchronous machines using this curve as default."@en;
                                                               rdfs:domain cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve;
                                                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                               rdfs:label "InitiallyUsedBySynchronousMachines"@en;
                                                               rdfs:range cim:SynchronousMachine.
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve.SynchronousMachines a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                rdfs:comment "Synchronous machines using this curve."@en;
                                                rdfs:domain cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                rdfs:label "SynchronousMachines"@en;
                                                rdfs:range cim:SynchronousMachine.
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve.coolantTemperature a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                               rdfs:comment "The machine's coolant temperature (e.g., ambient air or stator circulating water)."@en;
                                               rdfs:domain cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve;
                                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                               rdfs:label "coolantTemperature"@en;
                                               rdfs:range cim:Temperature.
cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve.hydrogenPressure a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                             rdfs:comment "The hydrogen coolant pressure."@en;
                                             rdfs:domain cim:ReactiveCapabilityCurve;
                                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                             rdfs:label "hydrogenPressure"@en;
                                             rdfs:range cim:Pressure.
cim:ReactivePower a rdfs:Datatype;
                  rdfs:comment "Product of RMS value of the voltage and the RMS value of the quadrature component of the current."@en;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                  rdfs:label "ReactivePower"@en;
                  owl:equivalentClass xsd:float;
                  cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Domain";
                  cimdoc:packageTier "Normative";
                  cimdoc:unitSymbol cim:UnitSymbol.VAr.
cim:RealEnergy a rdfs:Datatype;
               rdfs:comment "Real electrical energy."@en;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
               rdfs:label "RealEnergy"@en;
               owl:equivalentClass xsd:float;
               cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Domain";
               cimdoc:packageTier "Normative";
               cimdoc:unitSymbol cim:UnitSymbol.Wh.
cim:RecloseSequence a owl:Class;
                    rdfs:comment "A reclose sequence (open and close) is defined for each possible reclosure of a breaker."@en;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                    rdfs:label "RecloseSequence"@en;
                    rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject;
                    cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Protection";
                    cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RecloseSequence.recloseDelay a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Indicates the time lapse before the reclose step will execute a reclose."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:RecloseSequence;
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                 rdfs:label "recloseDelay"@en;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Seconds.
cim:RecloseSequence.recloseStep a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                rdfs:comment "Indicates the ordinal position of the reclose step relative to other steps in the sequence."@en;
                                rdfs:domain cim:RecloseSequence;
                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                rdfs:label "recloseStep"@en;
                                rdfs:range xsd:integer.
cim:Recloser a owl:Class;
             rdfs:comment "Pole-mounted fault interrupter with built-in phase and ground relays, current transformer (CT), and supplemental controls."@en;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
             rdfs:label "Recloser"@en;
             rdfs:subClassOf cim:ProtectedSwitch;
             cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
             cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegularIntervalSchedule a owl:Class;
                            rdfs:comment "The schedule has time points where the time between them is constant."@en;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "RegularIntervalSchedule"@en;
                            rdfs:subClassOf cim:BasicIntervalSchedule;
                            cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Core";
                            cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegularIntervalSchedule.TimePoints a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                       rdfs:comment "The regular interval time point data values that define this schedule."@en;
                                       rdfs:domain cim:RegularIntervalSchedule;
                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                       rdfs:label "TimePoints"@en;
                                       rdfs:range cim:RegularTimePoint.
cim:RegularIntervalSchedule.endTime a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                    rdfs:comment "The time for the last time point. The value can be a time of day, not a specific date."@en;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RegularIntervalSchedule;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "endTime"@en;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime.
cim:RegularIntervalSchedule.timeStep a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                     rdfs:comment "The time between each pair of subsequent regular time points in sequence order."@en;
                                     rdfs:domain cim:RegularIntervalSchedule;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                     rdfs:label "timeStep"@en;
                                     rdfs:range cim:Seconds.
cim:RegularTimePoint a owl:Class;
                     rdfs:comment "Time point for a schedule where the time between the consecutive points is constant."@en;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                     rdfs:label "RegularTimePoint"@en;
                     cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Core";
                     cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegularTimePoint.sequenceNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                    rdfs:comment "The position of the regular time point in the sequence. Note that time points don't have to be sequential, i.e. time points may be omitted. The actual time for a RegularTimePoint is computed by multiplying the associated regular interval schedule's time step with the regular time point sequence number and adding the associated schedules start time. To specify values for the start time, use sequence number 0. The sequence number cannot be negative."@en;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RegularTimePoint;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "sequenceNumber"@en;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:integer.
cim:RegularTimePoint.value1 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                            rdfs:comment "The first value at the time. The meaning of the value is defined by the derived type of the associated schedule."@en;
                            rdfs:domain cim:RegularTimePoint;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "value1"@en;
                            rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegularTimePoint.value2 a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                            rdfs:comment "The second value at the time. The meaning of the value is defined by the derived type of the associated schedule."@en;
                            rdfs:domain cim:RegularTimePoint;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                            rdfs:label "value2"@en;
                            rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegulatingCondEq a owl:Class;
                     rdfs:comment "A type of conducting equipment that can regulate a quantity (i.e. voltage or flow) at a specific point in the network."@en;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                     rdfs:label "RegulatingCondEq"@en;
                     rdfs:subClassOf cim:EnergyConnection;
                     cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                     cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegulatingCondEq.RegulatingControl a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                       rdfs:comment "The regulating control scheme in which this equipment participates."@en;
                                       rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingCondEq;
                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                       rdfs:label "RegulatingControl"@en;
                                       rdfs:range cim:RegulatingControl.
cim:RegulatingCondEq.controlEnabled a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                    rdfs:comment "Specifies the regulation status of the equipment. True is regulating, false is not regulating."@en;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingCondEq;
                                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                    rdfs:label "controlEnabled"@en;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:RegulatingControl a owl:Class;
                      rdfs:comment "Specifies a set of equipment that works together to control a power system quantity such as voltage or flow. Remote bus voltage control is possible by specifying the controlled terminal located at some place remote from the controlling equipment. The specified terminal shall be associated with the connectivity node of the controlled point. The most specific subtype of RegulatingControl shall be used in case such equipment participate in the control, e.g. TapChangerControl for tap changers. For flow control, load sign convention is used, i.e. positive sign means flow out from a TopologicalNode (bus) into the conducting equipment. The attribute minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue are required in the following cases: - For a power generating module operated in power factor control mode to specify maximum and minimum power factor values; - Whenever it is necessary to have an off center target voltage for the tap changer regulator. For instance, due to long cables to off shore wind farms and the need to have a simpler setup at the off shore transformer platform, the voltage is controlled from the land at the connection point for the off shore wind farm. Since there usually is a voltage rise along the cable, there is typical and overvoltage of up 3-4 kV compared to the on shore station. Thus in normal operation the tap changer on the on shore station is operated with a target set point, which is in the lower parts of the dead band. The attributes minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue are not related to the attribute targetDeadband and thus they are not treated as an alternative of the targetDeadband. They are needed due to limitations in the local substation controller. The attribute targetDeadband is used to prevent the power flow from move the tap position in circles (hunting) that is to be used regardless of the attributes minAllowedTargetValue and maxAllowedTargetValue."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "RegulatingControl"@en;
                      rdfs:subClassOf cim:PowerSystemResource;
                      cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                      cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegulatingControl.discrete a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                               rdfs:comment "The regulation is performed in a discrete mode. This applies to equipment with discrete controls, e.g. tap changers and shunt compensators."@en;
                               rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                               rdfs:label "discrete"@en;
                               rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:RegulatingControl.enabled a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                              rdfs:comment "The flag tells if regulation is enabled."@en;
                              rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                              rdfs:label "enabled"@en;
                              rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:RegulatingControl.maxAllowedTargetValue a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                            rdfs:comment "Maximum allowed target value (RegulatingControl.targetValue)."@en;
                                            rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                            rdfs:label "maxAllowedTargetValue"@en;
                                            rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegulatingControl.minAllowedTargetValue a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                            rdfs:comment "Minimum allowed target value (RegulatingControl.targetValue)."@en;
                                            rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                            rdfs:label "minAllowedTargetValue"@en;
                                            rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegulatingControl.mode a owl:ObjectProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "The regulating control mode presently available. This specification allows for determining the kind of regulation without need for obtaining the units from a schedule."@en;
                           rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                           rdfs:label "mode"@en;
                           rdfs:range cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.
cim:RegulatingControl.monitoredPhase a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                     rdfs:comment "Phase voltage controlling this regulator, measured at regulator location."@en;
                                     rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                     rdfs:label "monitoredPhase"@en;
                                     rdfs:range cim:PhaseCode.
cim:RegulatingControl.targetDeadband a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                     rdfs:comment """This is a deadband used with discrete control to avoid excessive update of controls like tap changers and shunt compensator banks while regulating. The units of those appropriate for the mode. The attribute shall be a positive value or zero. If RegulatingControl.discrete is set to \"false\", the RegulatingControl.targetDeadband is to be ignored. Note that for instance, if the targetValue is 100 kV and the targetDeadband is 2 kV the range is from 99 to 101 kV."""@en;
                                     rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                     rdfs:label "targetDeadband"@en;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegulatingControl.targetValue a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                  rdfs:comment "The target value specified for case input. This value can be used for the target value without the use of schedules. The value has the units appropriate to the mode attribute."@en;
                                  rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                  rdfs:label "targetValue"@en;
                                  rdfs:range xsd:float.
cim:RegulatingControl.targetValueUnitMultiplier a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                                rdfs:comment "Specify the multiplier for used for the targetValue."@en;
                                                rdfs:domain cim:RegulatingControl;
                                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                                rdfs:label "targetValueUnitMultiplier"@en;
                                                rdfs:range cim:UnitMultiplier.
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind a owl:Class;
                              rdfs:comment "The kind of regulation model. For example regulating voltage, reactive power, active power, etc."@en;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                              rdfs:label "RegulatingControlModeKind"@en;
                              owl:equivalentClass [a owl:Class ; 
                                                   owl:oneOf (cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.activePower
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.admittance
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.currentFlow
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.powerFactor
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.reactivePower
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.temperature
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.timeScheduled
                                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.voltage)];
                              cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                              cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.activePower a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                            cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                          rdfs:comment "Active power is specified."@en;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                          rdfs:label "activePower"@en;
                                          cimdoc:enumCode 1 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.admittance a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                           cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                         rdfs:comment "Admittance is specified."@en;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "admittance"@en;
                                         cimdoc:enumCode 4 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.currentFlow a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                            cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                          rdfs:comment "Current flow is specified."@en;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                          rdfs:label "currentFlow"@en;
                                          cimdoc:enumCode 3 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.powerFactor a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                            cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                          rdfs:comment "Power factor is specified."@en;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                          rdfs:label "powerFactor"@en;
                                          cimdoc:enumCode 7 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.reactivePower a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                            rdfs:comment "Reactive power is specified."@en;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                            rdfs:label "reactivePower"@en;
                                            cimdoc:enumCode 2 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.temperature a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                            cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                          rdfs:comment "Control switches on/off based on the local temperature (i.e., a thermostat)."@en;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                          rdfs:label "temperature"@en;
                                          cimdoc:enumCode 6 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.timeScheduled a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                              cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                            rdfs:comment "Control switches on/off by time of day. The times may change on the weekend, or in different seasons."@en;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                            rdfs:label "timeScheduled"@en;
                                            cimdoc:enumCode 5 .
cim:RegulatingControlModeKind.voltage a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                        cim:RegulatingControlModeKind;
                                      rdfs:comment "Voltage is specified."@en;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                      rdfs:label "voltage"@en;
                                      cimdoc:enumCode 0 .
cim:RegulationSchedule a owl:Class;
                       rdfs:comment "A pre-established pattern over time for a controlled variable, e.g., busbar voltage."@en;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                       rdfs:label "RegulationSchedule"@en;
                       rdfs:subClassOf cim:SeasonDayTypeSchedule;
                       cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.Base.Wires";
                       cimdoc:packageTier "Normative".
cim:RegulationSchedule.RegulatingControl a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                         rdfs:comment "Regulating controls that have this schedule."@en;
                                         rdfs:domain cim:RegulationSchedule;
                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                         rdfs:label "RegulatingControl"@en;
                                         rdfs:range cim:RegulatingControl.
cim:RegulationSchedule.VoltageControlZones a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                           rdfs:comment "A VoltageControlZone may have a voltage regulation schedule."@en;
                                           rdfs:domain cim:RegulationSchedule;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                           rdfs:label "VoltageControlZones"@en;
                                           rdfs:range cim:VoltageControlZone.
cim:RemedialActionScheme a owl:Class;
                         rdfs:comment "Remedial Action Scheme (RAS), Special Protection Schemes (SPS), System Protection Schemes (SPS) or System Integrity Protection Schemes (SIPS)."@en;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                         rdfs:label "RemedialActionScheme"@en;
                         rdfs:subClassOf cim:PowerSystemResource;
                         cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.InfIEC61970.InfSIPS";
                         cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
cim:RemedialActionScheme.Stage a owl:ObjectProperty;
                               rdfs:comment "A Remedial Action Scheme (RAS) consist of one or more stage that are trigger and execute protection action."@en;
                               rdfs:domain cim:RemedialActionScheme;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                               rdfs:label "Stage"@en;
                               rdfs:range cim:Stage.
cim:RemedialActionScheme.armed a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                               rdfs:comment "The status of the class set by operation or by signal. Optional field that will override other status fields."@en;
                               rdfs:domain cim:RemedialActionScheme;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                               rdfs:label "armed"@en;
                               rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:RemedialActionScheme.kind a owl:ObjectProperty;
                              rdfs:comment "Kind of Remedial Action Scheme (RAS)."@en;
                              rdfs:domain cim:RemedialActionScheme;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                              rdfs:label "kind"@en;
                              rdfs:range cim:RemedialActionSchemeKind.
cim:RemedialActionScheme.normalArmed a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                                     rdfs:comment "The default/normal value used when other active signal/values are missing."@en;
                                     rdfs:domain cim:RemedialActionScheme;
                                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                                     rdfs:label "normalArmed"@en;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
cim:RemedialActionSchemeKind a owl:Class;
                             rdfs:comment "Classification of Remedial Action Scheme."@en;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl>;
                             rdfs:label "RemedialActionSchemeKind"@en;
                             owl:equivalentClass [a owl:Class ; 
                                                  owl:oneOf (cim:RemedialActionSchemeKind.rAP
                                                             cim:RemedialActionSchemeKind.rAS)];
                             cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61970.InfIEC61970.InfSIPS";
                             cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
cim:RemedialActionSchemeKind.rAP a owl:NamedIndividual,
